{
  // What knip is here to catch, and — more to the point — what it is not.
  //
  // Run with no configuration it reports 112 findings on this repo, all of them
  // "exported but nothing imports it". That number is not a cleanup backlog,
  // because the category conflates three different things:
  //
  //   - genuinely dead code (three functions, deleted in the same commit as
  //     this file);
  //   - functions used inside their own module, where the fix is to drop the
  //     `export` keyword rather than the function — `hoursForTicket` in
  //     lib/sla/index.ts is called three times a few lines below its own
  //     declaration;
  //   - exports whose only consumer is not an import at all. `handlers` and
  //     `PLANNED_JOB_TYPES` in worker/handlers/index.ts are read by
  //     scripts/ci/repo-rules.mjs with a regex, so deleting them on knip's
  //     word would break the job-registry check that exists to keep the three
  //     job registries agreeing.
  //
  // Gating on that would mean either a 112-line ignore list — the "exemption
  // list" AGENTS.md says not to add your call site to — or a sweeping deletion
  // whose third case is actively wrong. So `exports` and `types` are excluded
  // and stay a thing somebody runs by hand: `npm run knip:exports`.
  //
  // What is left is gated because it is both meaningful and currently clean:
  // an unused dependency is supply-chain surface nobody is watching, and an
  // unlisted one is a build that works by luck through somebody else's
  // transitive tree. Both were at zero when this landed, so the check starts
  // green and stays cheap.
  "exclude": ["exports", "types", "nsExports", "nsTypes", "enumMembers"],
}
